    "body": "`execute_train` inserts serialized runtime environment JSON inside literal single quotes. An environment value such as `{\"RUN_NOTE\": \"owner's run\"}` makes Bash reject the command before Ray starts; paired apostrophes can instead be silently removed from the value.\n\nUse `shlex.quote` when passing `--runtime-env-json`. Add regressions that run the actual launcher through Bash with an argument-recording stand-in for the Ray CLI, covering both the `extra_env_vars` mapping and `ExecuteTrainConfig.extra_env_vars` JSON input. Register the tests in CPU CI and explicitly install the launcher's existing Typer dependency there.\n\nRelated: #2346 fixes equals signs in the space-separated input parser. This change covers the later shell serialization of the runtime environment.\n\nValidation on macOS arm64, Python 3.12.13:\n\n- Same 10 regression cases: **8 failed / 2 passed before**, **10 passed after**.\n- `python -m pytest tests/utils/test_runtime_env_quoting.py -q` and direct script execution both passed.\n- Repository-pinned pre-commit hooks on all four changed files and `git diff --check` passed; generated workflow matches its template.\n- Tests check the exact CLI arguments and decoded environment values. Ray cluster startup, GPU work, and model training are not exercised.\n\nPrepared with Codex assistance; validation results above were observed on the before/after implementations.\n",
